# Converted from corpus/flowcharts/0065.mmd by corpus/convert.py.
Admin IAM User -> Deploy IAM User: Creates
Deploy IAM User -> CloudFormation: Uses
"Bucket: Main Storage" -> review/
"Bucket: Main Storage" -> staging/
"Bucket: Main Storage" -> output/
"Bucket: Main Storage" -> aggregations/
EKS (3 Workers) -> Dask Dashboard Service: Exposes
Elastic Container Registry -> EKS (3 Workers): Serves images
CloudFormation -> Amazon S3 (Data Storage): Creates
CloudFormation -> EKS Cluster: Creates
CloudFormation -> CloudWatch: Creates
CloudFormation -> Elastic Container Registry: Creates
EKS (3 Workers) -> Amazon S3 (Data Storage): Data flow
EKS (3 Workers) -> CloudWatch: Logs & metrics
Staging Table -> Reporting Table: Aggregation
Amazon S3 (Data Storage) -> Snowflake (Data Warehousing): Copy data
EKS (3 Workers) -> Snowflake (Data Warehousing): Write partitions
End User -> Dask Dashboard Service: Logs in and monitors
Developer -> Git Repository: Commits changes
Git Repository -> CI/CD Pipeline: Triggers
CI/CD Pipeline -> Elastic Container Registry: "Build, Test, Push"
CI/CD Pipeline -> EKS (3 Workers): Update

US East (N. Virginia) Region { AWS Services, Snowflake (Data Warehousing), Legend, End User }
AWS Services { IAM, Amazon S3 (Data Storage), EKS Cluster, CloudWatch, CloudFormation, Elastic Container Registry }
IAM { Admin IAM User, Deploy IAM User }
Amazon S3 (Data Storage) { "Bucket: Main Storage", review/, staging/, output/, aggregations/ }
EKS Cluster { EKS (3 Workers), Dask Dashboard Service }
CloudWatch { Logs, Metrics, Alarms }
Snowflake (Data Warehousing) { Staging Table, Reporting Table }
Legend { "EKS: Main cost consideration" }
External Deployment { Git Repository, CI/CD Pipeline, Developer }
